--- stdout
## rust-doctor → code scanning: published 6 of 9 result(s)

Withheld (below the `--fail-on warning` gate, so they never failed anything; the full SARIF
is in the `rust-doctor-sarif` artifact and `scripts/doctor.sh --findings` prints locally):

- `excessive-clone` × 2 (note)
- `skipped-pass` × 1 (note)

**Paths that were not in this tree.** A re-anchored one is published against the crate
manifest, so the alert links somewhere real but not where the tool said; anything else is
published as-is and will not link to code at all:

- cargo_common_metadata: ambiguous across crates (., jdwp-client, mcp-server): Cargo.toml
- hardcoded-secrets: absolute path outside the workspace: /somewhere/else/src/main.rs
- multiple_crate_versions: re-anchored to mcp-server/Cargo.toml
- panic-in-library: no such file under the workspace root or any crate: nowhere/at/all.rs
- result-unit-error: no such file under the workspace root or any crate: totally_made_up.rs

